ile developing their own line.\n\nReason:\nPlaying at **I8** is the optimal move.\n1.  **Defense:** It directly blocks the gap between Black\'s stones (H8 and J8), preventing Black from forming a dangerous solid three-in-a-row.\n2.  **Offense:** It connects vertically with White\'s existing stone at I9, forming a continuous line of two stones ("Live 2"). This allows White to transition from defense to building their own threats.\nAny other move allows Black to take I8, resulting in a strong advantage for the opponent.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "I", "row": 8}'}
